A when that tests an optional field's presence and reads it. Reading it
already restricts the lacuna to the instances that have it, and to test
presence alone the field is named bare.
-- ship/history/0.0.thema --
schema: {
	name:   string
	count?: int
}
-- ship/1.0.thema --
schema: {
	name:  string
	count: int
}

ForwardLens: {
	v0_0: _
	v1_0: {
		count: orelse(v0_0.count, 0)
	}
	lacunas: {
		count: [{
			type:    PrecisionLoss
			message: "counts above 1000 are rounded downstream"
			when:    v0_0.count != _|_ && v0_0.count > 1000
		}]
	}
}
-- out/error --
a condition reading v0_0.count concerns only the instances that have it, so its presence need not be tested; to test presence alone, write when: v0_0.count:
    1.0.thema:15:13
